---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'workflow', label: 'Workflow' },
   { id: 'resume', label: 'Resume and hints' },
   { id: 'claims', label: 'Evidence claims' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Audit a full site with an agent"
   summary="The full-site-audit skill drives desktop assessment procedures through a durable coordinator, with observed states, complete journeys, current evidence, and explicit coverage gaps."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="panel" id="workflow">
      <h2>Workflow</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>The agent reuses your target, scope, WCAG profile, and authorized actions.</li>
         <li>For websites, it discovers pages and links the inventory with <code>a1 audit run --inventory</code>.</li>
         <li>It observes page or app states and registers ordered user journeys.</li>
         <li>It claims each procedure with <code>audit next</code>, performs its actions, records current evidence, and evaluates the check. Reader procedures require VoiceOver or NVDA when the procedure specifies a real reader.</li>
         <li>It resolves coverage gaps before finalization and builds website reports. Draft reports remain available during the assessment.</li>
      </ol>
      <pre><code>a1 audit discover https://createdbyfireside.com --scope site \
   --out .a11ied/fireside/inventory.json
a1 audit run https://createdbyfireside.com --environment environment.json \
   --inventory .a11ied/fireside/inventory.json --json
a1 audit next .a11ied/fireside/run.json --json</code></pre>
      <p>
         Install the repository's <code>full-site-audit</code> skill through the same
         <a href="/guides/agent-skill">agent skill package</a> as the component development skill.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="resume">
      <h2>Resume and hints</h2>
      <p>
         Runtime commands own the inventory and assessment state. The agent reads
         <code>audit status</code> after interruption and preserves the run's evidence paths.
         <code>audit resume</code> blocks interrupted work; explicit retries follow restoration
         of a safe UI state. Changed observations revoke old proof. Site hints are hypotheses
         to check against the current product, not completed assessments.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="claims">
      <h2>Evidence claims</h2>
      <p>
         To view an unfinished assessment, use <code>a1 report build --draft</code> with
         the run's inventory, page results, and output paths. The draft shows available
         results and pending checks without marking the assessment complete. The MCP
         <code>report_build</code> tool accepts <code>draft: true</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
         Unassessed pages stay marked not tested. A partial crawl stays a partial inventory.
         The report retains recorded procedures, outcomes, evidence notes, and pointers. It
         reports accepted behavioral judgments with their provenance and artifacts. A passing automated result
         is not reported as full WCAG conformance.
      </p>
      <p>
         Virtual observations remain simulated. <code>cantTell</code>, missing capabilities,
         blocked journeys, and incomplete discovery remain unresolved. Native app assessment
         can use the coordinator, but report publication requires a website inventory.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
